From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:59:18 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 17/27] Plutonium: agents drive windows and tabs

- T3's MCP server offers native window tools (launch_app, list_windows,
  snapshot_window, click_window, type_window, press_window, scroll_window,
  drag_window, ...) to every provider, in a Plutonium session only. T3
  declares them as a toolkit and each acts as the calling thread
  (McpToolAccess); the Plutonium helper runs them for that thread's tag
  (POST /v1/threads/<tag>/mcp/call). A helper older than the tools says so
  instead of "Not found.". Tabs stay T3's preview tools. Claude no longer
  gets the helper's stdio MCP server as well.
- The desktop browser channel's `open` and `close`: a server tab no shell
  page shows is opened by the helper (tagged with its thread) and attached
  at once, instead of a 10 s wait and a headless tab; the helper closes it
  when its preview closes. A shell page that shows the thread adopts it.
  Such a tab starts blank, so the server navigates it to the first URL.
- A page the mini player shows is laid out at the size it last had (1280x800
  if it was never shown) and scaled down, as in the Electron build, not at
  the player's 320x200.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
